  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3269ab77e5738674b9fefab358f453ff, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::UIAnimLab.Station
  Code: 
  Title: 07  Inspector and Authoring
  Summary: 'Everything about editing animations in the Inspector: step headers, the
    grouped Type and Ease menus, the one-button rows, what + gives you, copy and
    paste, mirroring, the warnings a broken step shows, and the pop-out window. Most
    of these are about what you see in the Inspector, so the stage is often just
    there to play on.


    <b>Using this board:</b> select a tile. Its Inspector
    shows these directions at the top, with Select buttons for the objects to watch,
    and its UI Animation Player underneath. Badges in a tile''s corner say what it
    needs: <color=#FF9E5E>PREVIEW</color> (the Play buttons, out of play mode), <color=#FF9E5E>PLAY
    MODE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>INSPECTOR</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>SCENE VIEW</color>,
    <color=#FF9E5E>CONSOLE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>POP-OUT</color> (an animation''s
    own window).


    In play mode: right-drag pans, the wheel zooms, Tab steps
    through tiles, Home shows them all.'
  Watch: 
  WatchObjects: []
  HowTo: 
  Expect: 
  Needs: 0
  Style: 2
  WikiPage: 
  Capture: 
  Width: 620
  StageHeight: 0
